From 0ffe51d763573b60525b37ebe7ba6d09135ca1b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:52:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: borders, lines, list bullets, focus rings and text
 lines through OpenGPU

GraphicsContextOpenGPU now draws itself the calls it used to hand to cairo
whole (cairo-out item 3, gfopenbrowser docs/STEP5-6-WEBCORE.md). Each
one does what WebKit's Cairo:: code for it does:

- drawRect (Cairo::drawRect): the rectangle filled with the fill colour
  (fillRectWithColor: nothing for an invisible colour over), then a
  1-pixel stroke of the stroke colour half a pixel inside it, with the
  context's caps, joins and dashes.
- drawLine (Cairo::drawLine, borders): a line centred across its
  thickness, drawn without anti-aliasing as cairo's. A solid line under 1
  pixel is drawn 1 wide. Dotted and dashed lines get their filled corners
  and the dash pattern balanced between them (cairo's corner, pattern and
  offset arithmetic).
- drawEllipse (Cairo::drawEllipse, list bullets): filled with the fill
  colour when visible, then stroked at the stroke thickness. The path is
  WebCore's four-cubic ellipse.
- drawLinesForText (underlines, overlines, line-through): rectangles of
  the stroke colour on the line's box. The origin is on whole device
  pixels (x rounded, y up), at least half a pixel thick, fainter under a
  scale below 1, and double lines get a second row.
- Focus rings: with the Adwaita theme (the engine's build), what
  GraphicsContextCairo does, Adwaita::paintFocus, which draws through
  this context's own calls.

None of these draws a shadow or the global alpha, as cairo's don't. When
OpenGPU can't take one part (blending, a size past the fixed point), that
part is drawn on cairo after the batch, as cairo would have drawn it.
Spelling and grammar markers (drawErrorUnderline's squiggle) stay
cairo's.
---
 .../graphics/amiga/GraphicsContextOpenGPU.cpp | 269 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../graphics/amiga/GraphicsContextOpenGPU.h   |  12 +-
